      "revision": "4a624fd75a4bc64720c9780a5854e832cd75ebde",
      "reply": {
        "answer": "Pulse-Doppler radar measures range by timing and closure by Doppler shift, using the shift to reject clutter and track targets in velocity [1, 5]. Pulse repetition frequency (PRF) determines unambiguous range and velocity measurement capabilities, with higher PRFs providing excellent velocity resolution but causing range ambiguity [6]. Additionally, a radar warning receiver (RWR) detects radar signals to show a threat's type, mode, and rough relative bearing [3, 5].",
